# Datagrams that are not well-formed BACnet/IPv6. None may panic; a length
# field that disagrees with the datagram is kept, so the sender can be found.

82 01 => error truncated 4/2
81 0a 00 04 => error not-bacnet-ipv6 129
82 02 00 06 00 02 => error truncated 7/6
82 00 00 0a 00 02 57 00 00 00 => error wrong-length 0/3
82 03 00 09 00 02 57 00 00 => error wrong-length 3/2
82 01 00 09 00 02 57 00 00 => error wrong-length 1/2
82 08 00 0b 00 02 57 fe 80 00 00 => error wrong-length 8/4
82 06 00 08 00 02 57 00 => error wrong-length 6/1
82 02 00 20 00 02 57 01 00 10 08 => original-broadcast from 000257 npdu 01001008 (length 32, datagram 11)
